KG42.register("clusters-a3190d50e76e2da4e23c9bf4",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v142-d-K003","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","label":"Parameter setting, information acquisition, and settlement of non-collaborative hierarchical billing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Parameter setting, information acquisition, and settlement of non-collaborative hierarchical billing","market_meaning":"The aggregator sets the penalty factor in advance and updates iterative information such as total energy consumption and average energy consumption, and customers obtain the required inputs; settlement applies the base or penalty rate according to the customer's position relative to average energy consumption, and separately retains the cost-balance branch where the penalty factor equals 1 and the heavy-load charging branch where it is greater than 1.","mechanism_ids":["M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The three Rule-Chains belong to the same non-collaborative hierarchical billing mechanism. The conditions of below or equal to the mean, exceeding the mean, and different penalty factors apply separately; obtaining information round by round does not equal completing actual settlement round by round, and the existing Rule-Chains also do not contain a complete game solution.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Mean and penalty factor directly enter the billing branches, and information supply and charging duties can jointly express one rule. The transaction response in the numerical comparison forms another cluster, and observed trends are not incorporated into general billing obligations.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the aggregator's information update, penalty factor setting, and average energy consumption definition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the customer-side information requirement to obtain the wholesale price function, total quantity, and mean value round by round."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the hierarchical charging formula and the payment and cost allocation conclusions under each penalty factor condition."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E18"],"rationale":"The source places the information update of the aggregator and ECS and the customer acquisition of information in the same iterative process; the two Rule-Chains respectively provide the supply activity and the acquisition requirement."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::theta-alpha","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::theta_alpha","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The penalty factor set in advance and the average energy consumption definition correspond respectively to the rate multiplier and the segment threshold of the hierarchical bill, and no new parameter-tuning decision or dynamic update formula is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18"],"rationale":"The acquired total energy consumption and mean correspond to the input contents of the billing base rate and threshold; this is a functional correspondence between information and the billing function, and it does not imply that every iteration produces a settled bill."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The same M02 aggregator sets the penalty factor, exchanges information, and undertakes the stated payment duties; only a common node display representative is selected."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::theta-alpha","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_alpha"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The same definition clearly links the penalty factor set in advance with the hierarchical bill multiplier; the setting duty and the settlement parameter role are each retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::x_i_tot","v141-c-R010::x::x_i_tot"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The same M02 customer time-period total energy consumption participates respectively in statistical information and bill calculation. Retain each Rule-Chain's unit record, feasible domain description, and local use, and do not override field differences because of the same object identifier."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M04","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The textual requirement and the tuple expression describe the same round-by-round information acquisition obligation; the latter is an equivalent translation candidate, both original objects are retained, and they are not counted as two independent requirements."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Both billing branches divide by total energy consumption; the existing M02 quotation and the frozen Rule-Chain do not give a definition for the case where total energy consumption is zero, nor do they explicitly exclude this case. A strictly positive condition cannot be imported from other mechanisms, nor can a continuous extension be stipulated on one's own.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify the applicable domain or the zero-total handling in the source and add it to C; before handling, do not claim that the bill is mathematically closed over all feasible dispatches."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Information acquisition originally served the customer subgradient iteration, but the current C directory has no M02 payoff function, equilibrium conditions, or solution Rule-Chain for Equation (14); this cluster cannot replace the complete process from non-collaborative scheduling to final settlement.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If it is required to connect through equilibrium solving, upstream supplements the payoff, equilibrium, and iteration Rule-Chains of the same mechanism; retain the quantities already existing in R007, and do not repeatedly add objects according to its revised text."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The hierarchical bill and the base and penalty rates are still carried by generic settlement and coordination nodes, and the related ontology proposals have not been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g04-e06"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P02","v141-b-g02-p01","v141-b-g04-p01"],"required_work":"Manual inspection should examine the boundary between bill structure and rate concepts and the overlap of proposals; before approval, only the existing frozen objects are cited."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B basis for the hierarchical bill, parameter setting, and information exchange remains unverified, and has not undergone the independent source audit omitted in this experiment or the C2 independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g02-e13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original formulas, conditions, and communication descriptions, maintaining the current source status and candidate nature."}]},"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R007","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R008","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-1494fb13645c04a4","COMP-d839969e92ed0c6e","COMP-ebd853401562a305"]});
